  "2. Memory: cycle H's peak_rss_bytes is 6,661,980,160; release's 7G cap is 1.13 times that, under step 5's 1.15. If the worker reads the same, raise release's MemoryMax (7.5G) before 2b. The release loop peaked at 6.1 GB (1.23). Derive peaked at 4.6 GB (4,394 MiB, 86 % of its 5G cap) on ticks mixing project and parse units, without the inventory.",
  "3. Staged history: step C took 12.4 to 14.0 s (5.8 s in the first run, 8.2 s in the review's run), A 2.1 s, chunks at most 2.8 s; all under the 30 s target.",
  "4. The first run's finding 4 stands: G's cycle made 13 requests and H's 93 from the same copy; 15 of 35 acquire ticks ended their pass before 200 of 240 s (median 30 requests, range 7 to 53).",
  "5. A killed build counts toward the build interval (D-0199 counts admitted attempts): after the kill at 66 min, release deferred at 93 and 124 min. In production a build killed at release's cap delays the next by 6 h.",
  "6. derive_one's own top-level write is now the claim, so a kill 'inside derive_one' lands in the claim and leaves only the run; the extra kill inside a unit's output write left an attempt and admission, which the next tick closed as a counted process_interrupted (unit ready on its backoff); the kill in the admission left the lease, which the next tick settled (died_unclaimed)."
